Written to `reviews/2-security-redteam.md` (316 lines, ~40 findings). No existing files modified.

Headline findings, by attack surface:

**Cross-tenant:** `tasks/get`→`queue_jobs` has no specified tenant check (S1.1) — a `task_id` yields an export signed URL. `resolveTenant` never verifies the resolved team's `organization_id` matches the delegation's org (S1.2). Tenant auto-provisioning is ungated (S1.3). Tenant filtering rests on a lint rule with no runtime backstop (S1.5).

**Three-header auth:** `X-Nessie-Context` verification checks neither `aud` nor `iss`, yet shares a key set with DeepWater/DeepSignal — cross-service token confusion and agent-identity spoofing (S2.1). No jti/nonce binding means provenance is replayable for 300 s (S2.2). `REQUIRE_AUTH=false` serves a fixed omnipotent dev principal with well-known ids and no prod guard (S2.3). The `tv` epoch claim is verified but never enforced — a dead control (S2.4).

**Approvals (F6):** `arguments_hash` canonicalisation is entirely unspecified (S3.1), token consumption is never stated to be tenant/tool/args-bound (S3.2), approver role comes solely from a claim DeepCRM doesn't issue and `required_role: owner` silently degrades to admin (S3.3), pending rows are uncapped with full argument snapshots (S3.4).

**Policy/redaction — the largest cluster:** `display_name` is denormalised from the primary attribute regardless of sensitivity and leaks through every `RecordSummary` (S5.1). `_n.<slug>` shadow keys inside `data` aren't covered by the documented redaction (S5.2). Merge/delete `snapshot` pre-images enter `record_changes` while feed/webhook redaction language covers only `old_value`/`new_value` (S5.3). `crm_record_at`/history redaction undefined (S5.4). Duplicate-candidate evidence echoes values (S4.4). `restore`/`unlink` have no policy default at all (S4.1).

**SSRF/exfil:** webhook SSRF is checked at registration, not delivery — DNS-rebind TOCTOU (S6.1). Critically, `crm_webhook_set` is admin-only but **not approval-gated**, and new/re-enabled webhooks replay the full never-deleted change history evaluated as admin — an exfiltration channel that bypasses the export approval gate entirely (S6.2). Export itself doesn't specify whether the approval message reflects the requested restricted-attribute projection (S6.3). The webhook secret is "shown once" — to the agent, in model context (S7.1).

**DoS/audit:** unbounded recursive `Filter` grammar (S9.1), no `.max()` on bulk rows and ~6–10 MB possible per record (S9.2), trigram matching at threshold 0.3 inside lock-holding write transactions (S9.3), idempotency replays returning results shaped for the *original* caller's redaction context (S9.5), audit chain forks under concurrency with no anchor and no denial auditing (S8.1).

The doc includes per-finding doc+section citations, attack scenarios, concrete fixes, and a severity-ranked summary table.
